# Augment Guidelines

Follow these repository requirements in every Agent and Chat session.

## Database

- Database schema changes must be generated by command.
- Apply migrations by command.
- Check migration status after applying.
- Run build after migration work.
- Never hand-write schema migrations.
- Never use `synchronize: true`.

Commands:

```bash
npm run db:local:migration:generate -- src/database/migrations/DescriptiveMigrationName
npm run db:local:migration:deploy
npm run db:local:migration:status
npm run build
```

## Modules

- New business modules must include DTOs, controller, repository, service layer, and module file.
- Controllers must not access TypeORM directly.
- Split services by operation group when behavior is more than trivial: get/query, create, update, delete.

## Type Safety

- Avoid `any`.
- Prefer DTOs, interfaces, entity types, `unknown`, generics, or narrow union types.
- Only use `any` when unavoidable, after narrowing/validation, and with a short explanatory comment.
